  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> is the gravitational potential due to sphere of uniform density on its surface, then its value at the centre of sphere will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>V</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>V</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The magnitude of gravitational potential of a solid sphere at a distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;from the centre is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>At&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></math>.</p><p>At&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Clearly,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>V</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.</p></blockquote>"
  }
